  "slug": "artist:mulatu-astatke",
  "name": "Mulatu Astatke",
  "editorial_article": "Mulatu Astatke is an Ethiopian musician and arranger who, in 1966, recorded his debut albums Afro-Latin Soul, Volumes 1 & 2 in New York City. Trained at the Trinity College of Music in London and the Berklee College of Music in Boston, he introduced the vibraphone and conga drums to Ethiopian popular music. His development of Ethio-jazz, a fusion of traditional Ethiopian music with American jazz, funk, and soul, reached a peak with the 1974 release Yekatit Ethio Jazz on Amha Records. After the fall of the Derg regime, his career gained significant international momentum through the 1998 reissuing of his work on the Buda Musique compilation Éthiopiques Volume 4. His composition Tezeta was used in the 2024 film Nickel Boys, and he has collaborated with artists including The Heliocentrics and the Either/Orchestra.",
